    "description": "Zebra Technologies MP70X1 & MP70X2 scanner scales: a family of self-indicating, weight-only, single or dual-interval, non-automatic weighing instruments. May be used for direct sales to the public. Designed for flush-mounting in checkout surface, with frame extensions to support the instrument in the checkout counter; steel framework supporting one load cell, barcode scanner and electronics; stainless steel load receptor; single (MX-201) or dual (MX-202) pole-mounted display; optional Produce Flip-Up Bar Platter to weigh oversize objects; optional Customer Side Scanner (CSS). Designed for permanent installation in checkout surface, so no level indicator required; the medium size model may be fitted with adjustable feet. Platform dimensions: Medium 398 mm x 292 mm; Long 506 mm x 292 mm. Devices: initial zero setting device, semi-automatic zero setting device, zero tracking device, automatic zero setting device, zero indicator, gravity compensation. Sealing: load cell model and serial number stored in scanner secure memory and checked at boot-up; non-resettable C and P counters must be written on a tamper-evident label on or near the rating plate; scale modules 20-MP7-M30-02 and 20-MP7-M30-04 have a calibration switch under a screw on the U-bar sealed with a wire or plastic seal or a tamper-evident label. Optional EAS Security Tag Deactivation antenna may be fitted beneath the platter weighing surface."
